  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Empty Bottle in Chicago, Illinois, on Friday, November 1, 2002 [1][2]. This event is the 36th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a performance at Bottom of the Hill on October 23, 2002 [2]. The available recording is an audience capture that lasts 57 minutes and includes 17 songs [1]. The setlist opens with “The Alphonse Mambo” and “Source Decay” before moving to “We Were Patriots,” a track with 12 archived performances [1][2]. “Send me an Angel” appears next, marking its first appearance in 26 archived shows after a gap of 2,242 days [1][2]. The band plays “Jenny,” “Snow Crush Killing Song,” and “Black Molly” before introducing “Palmcorder Yajna,” which is first in the archive [1][2]. “Tollund Man” and “Alpha Double Negative: Going to Catalina” follow, the latter being a rare track with 12 archived performances [1][2]. The set continues with “Baboon,” “Shadow Song,” and “No Children.” A highlight is “Closer, Imports,” which is first in the archive and legendary as the only archived performance of the song [1][2]. The show concludes with “See America Right,” a cover of “The Sign” by Ace of Base, and “The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton” [1]. This audience recording is the only available capture of the event [1].",
